    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0170" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg78"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Marshal Stalin to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d114-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-10">November 10, 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret message from Premier J. V. Stalin to President Franklin D.
                    Roosevelt</p>
                <p>I have received Your message of November 8th.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d114-f2"/> I
                    thank You for Your answer.</p>
                <p>Your plan concerning the organization of our meeting in Iran, I accept. I hope,
                    and [<hi rendition="#italic">that</hi>] Mr. Churchill will agree with this
                    proposal.</p>
                <pb facs="0171" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/>
                <p>By November 22nd, Mr. V. M. Molotov and our military representative will arrive
                    in Cairo, where together with you they will agree upon everything necessary in
                    connection with our meeting in Iran.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">November</hi> 10, 1943.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d114-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d114-f1-content">
